WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.097
- All right, well when it comes to mommy,

00:00:02.097 --> 00:00:04.297
our next two guests know
how to roll with the punches

00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:07.228
and find humor in the most
ridiculous of situations.

00:00:07.228 --> 00:00:09.317
Let's welcome back the ladies behind the,

00:00:09.317 --> 00:00:11.108
"I mom so hard" podcast,

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:14.063
Kristen Hensley and Jen Smedley, y'all.

00:00:14.063 --> 00:00:15.965
(audience cheering)

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:19.215
(upbeat country music)

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.089
I'm not allowed to hug yet, still.

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:29.480
Like, what's up?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.056
- We're elbow bumping. We're doing it all-

00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:32.285
- [Kelly] Oh wait, this is yours.

00:00:32.285 --> 00:00:33.118
- Is that me, though?

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:34.266
- [Kelly] This is yours.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.546
- I mean, I have to drive home, though.

00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:36.379
- You're classy.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:38.437
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, really? Me too.

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:40.538
- I don't like red wine. That's why.

00:00:40.538 --> 00:00:41.371
- Oh, you don't?

00:00:41.371 --> 00:00:42.789
- I just, I, it's okay.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:44.102
- It's good for your heart, I guess.

00:00:44.102 --> 00:00:46.101
- Yeah, I know it's good for
you, I just don't like it.

00:00:46.101 --> 00:00:47.290
- It's good for my attitude.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.861
- [Kelly] I don't drink it
because it's good for my heart.

00:00:48.861 --> 00:00:50.261
- [Zooey] It means we're like, thirsty.

00:00:50.261 --> 00:00:51.220
It's kind of weird.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.050
- That's the whole, it does,
and then you drink a little bit

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.262
and you're like, I'm really good at darts.

00:00:54.262 --> 00:00:55.095
- I don't want to mix water.

00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:55.928
(laughter)

00:00:55.928 --> 00:00:57.843
- I'm really good at darts?

00:00:57.843 --> 00:00:58.767
- [Kristen] Yep.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:00:59.825
- [Kelly] but y'all have been busy.

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:01.697
- We have been, well, the
kids are back in school,

00:01:01.697 --> 00:01:02.794
which is fantastic-

00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:03.627
- Woohoo

00:01:03.627 --> 00:01:04.460
- Yay!

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.193
(audience cheers)

00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:08.626
- Yeah, which you'd think
would give us time to shower,

00:01:08.626 --> 00:01:09.459
but that not-

00:01:09.459 --> 00:01:10.292
- No.

00:01:10.292 --> 00:01:11.428
- really happening that much either.

00:01:11.428 --> 00:01:12.261
- [Kelly] Yeah. You're catching up.

00:01:12.261 --> 00:01:13.345
- Yeah, just so much from the last,

00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:16.058
And we're finally back on
tour because all the shows

00:01:16.058 --> 00:01:18.776
we had in 2020 got pushed,
so we're so excited.

00:01:18.776 --> 00:01:20.068
- [Kelly] That's really cool.

00:01:20.068 --> 00:01:20.901
- [Jen] Yeah.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:21.748
- [Kelly] Life is coming back.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.581
- Yes.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:23.806
- Life is coming back.

00:01:23.806 --> 00:01:24.639
- We need it

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:26.023
It's the it's called "the getaway tour."

00:01:26.023 --> 00:01:28.103
'Cause we felt like this
was a perfect opportunity

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:30.391
for us to get away from our families.

00:01:30.391 --> 00:01:31.224
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:34.273
And enjoy a night out, and
if it becomes five nights,

00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:37.031
that is your prerogative
and here's to you.

00:01:37.031 --> 00:01:37.903
- [Kelly] Dealer's choice.

00:01:37.903 --> 00:01:39.743
- Dealer's choice. No judgment.

00:01:39.743 --> 00:01:40.743
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:40.743 --> 00:01:43.097
- Um, well, it's, it's just a fact

00:01:43.097 --> 00:01:44.899
as awesome as it is to be a momma...

00:01:44.899 --> 00:01:47.010
It's damn hard work people.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.392
Especially during the
holidays it can be chaotic.

00:01:49.392 --> 00:01:51.082
'Cause we want to create
something magic for your kids.

00:01:51.082 --> 00:01:52.352
It all doesn't pan out sometimes.

00:01:52.352 --> 00:01:54.570
Um, whenever we have Kristen and Jen here,

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.082
we invite our audience to
share their comedy of errors,

00:01:57.082 --> 00:02:00.752
raising kids with a
round of wine to mommy.

00:02:00.752 --> 00:02:03.818
So we're all enjoying a
glass from Duckhorn vineyards

00:02:03.818 --> 00:02:05.415
the go-to wine at the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:02:05.415 --> 00:02:06.248
And it's delish.

00:02:06.248 --> 00:02:07.081
- [Kristen] Mm.

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:08.747
And we are ready for some real talk about

00:02:08.747 --> 00:02:10.719
getting through the most
wonderful time of the year.

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:12.689
So let's start with Ashley.

00:02:12.689 --> 00:02:15.759
What's going on in your mom world? Ashley.

00:02:15.759 --> 00:02:16.650
(audience claps)

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.050
Oh you're adorable.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.540
- Hi Kelly. My name is Ashley.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:20.373
I'm a mom of two, and last year

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.666
I didn't explain the whole Santa thing

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:25.255
to my daughter, who was three.

00:02:25.255 --> 00:02:27.945
So Christmas morning she
wakes up under the tree,

00:02:27.945 --> 00:02:29.999
there's all these Christmas
presents, and she's like,

00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:31.399
"where are these come from?"

00:02:31.399 --> 00:02:34.300
And I told her, "oh, this
man comes down the chimney.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.839
And he leaves presents for you."

00:02:35.839 --> 00:02:37.610
And she's like, "mom, it's Corona Virus!

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.391
Um, I don't know if he's vaccinated.

00:02:39.391 --> 00:02:41.420
I don't think people can come
into our homes right now."

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.270
- [Kelly] And you just said
a man comes down you chimney.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.851
- Well we say he's a
Healthcare worker, so.

00:02:44.851 --> 00:02:46.393
(audience laughs)

00:02:46.393 --> 00:02:47.226
- Vaccinated last Christmas-

00:02:47.226 --> 00:02:48.769
- [Ashley] She's not
really a fan of Santa,

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:50.198
and, or Christmas.

00:02:50.198 --> 00:02:51.582
I'm going to try again this year.

00:02:51.582 --> 00:02:52.982
So my question is, how do you

00:02:52.982 --> 00:02:55.215
explain Santa to your children?

00:02:55.215 --> 00:02:56.048
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:02:56.048 --> 00:02:56.896
- [Zooey] Well I have one.

00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:57.736
- This is tricky for me.

00:02:57.736 --> 00:03:01.195
I have one. You say,
Santa's left, present,

00:03:01.195 --> 00:03:03.195
Oh, he left them on the balcony,

00:03:03.195 --> 00:03:04.835
which is what he did for us.

00:03:04.835 --> 00:03:06.485
I don't know if you
guys put the request in,

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:07.415
but like outdoor-

00:03:07.415 --> 00:03:08.248
- We're not connected.

00:03:08.248 --> 00:03:09.081
- Oh.

00:03:09.081 --> 00:03:10.274
- [Zooey] you just put
the request in to Santa.

00:03:10.274 --> 00:03:14.042
You say Santa, I want them on my balcony.

00:03:14.042 --> 00:03:14.875
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:03:14.875 --> 00:03:15.708
- [Zooey] yeah.

00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:17.202
- The balcony? What do you do?

00:03:17.202 --> 00:03:18.557
- Yeah. Well, not that.

00:03:18.557 --> 00:03:19.789
(audience laughs)

00:03:19.789 --> 00:03:20.622
- [Kelly] Once again-

00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:21.906
- I'm learning a lot right now.

00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:24.997
You're really leading me to
some better decisions overall.

00:03:24.997 --> 00:03:26.974
I really need to get my admin together,

00:03:26.974 --> 00:03:29.127
but I'll tell you I'm
impressed that your little one

00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:31.615
has even the wherewithal
to think all those things.

00:03:31.615 --> 00:03:34.075
And I think they have
a bright future in HR.

00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:35.034
If I was going to say.

00:03:35.034 --> 00:03:35.867
(audience laughs)

00:03:35.867 --> 00:03:38.103
it sounds like they're really
smart and rule followers.

00:03:38.103 --> 00:03:39.802
- Yeah, or like the legal professions.

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:41.813
- Yeah, legal, maybe
like a City Inspector.

00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:42.646
- Totally.

00:03:42.646 --> 00:03:43.479
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:44.312
Yes.

00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:45.145
- Like a comptroller or something.

00:03:45.145 --> 00:03:45.978
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:45.978 --> 00:03:49.529
The future is bright for
your, your, your Santa goer.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.460
- [Zooey] Yeah.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.529
- [Kelly] what do you
do? Do you say anything?

00:03:52.529 --> 00:03:53.362
Do you say-

00:03:53.362 --> 00:03:56.001
- Well, the hardest thing
to explain to my kids was,

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:58.488
why there's a Santa at every mall.

00:03:58.488 --> 00:04:01.180
And I'm like, well, Santa is magical.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.911
There's one Santa, but
he has all these helpers.

00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:07.609
Yeah. And if I had the resources
and that kind of money,

00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:10.539
I'd be really magical
too. If I had all that,

00:04:10.539 --> 00:04:11.881
I'd be able to pull everything off.

00:04:11.881 --> 00:04:13.172
(audience laughs)

00:04:13.172 --> 00:04:14.508
- Thank you so much Ashley.

00:04:14.508 --> 00:04:15.341
(audience clapping)

00:04:15.341 --> 00:04:16.174
- [Kelly] Great question!

00:04:16.174 --> 00:04:17.007
- [Zooey] Great question!

00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:18.021
- Complicated stuff.

00:04:18.021 --> 00:04:20.058
- [Kelly] Complicated, complicated.

00:04:20.058 --> 00:04:20.891
(audience cheers)

00:04:20.891 --> 00:04:23.329
- We've been swapping
hilarious mommy fails

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.649
and some impressive mom
wins with the audience.

00:04:25.649 --> 00:04:27.817
Uh, so let's keep this
thing going, shall we?

00:04:27.817 --> 00:04:29.388
- [Kelly] Let's start with Stephanie.

00:04:29.388 --> 00:04:31.598
Stephanie, what's going
on in your mama world?

00:04:31.598 --> 00:04:32.431
(audience cheers)

00:04:32.431 --> 00:04:34.231
- [Zooey] Woo, woo, woo,
Stephanie, yeah, yeah, she's-

00:04:34.231 --> 00:04:37.169
- I'm a first time mom of an
adorable 2-and-a-half-year old

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:38.002
- [Ladies on Stage] Ohhhh.

00:04:38.002 --> 00:04:38.835
- [Stephanie] Thank you.

00:04:38.835 --> 00:04:41.610
And my husband and I are
both business owners.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.792
We're operating our first retail
store this holiday season.

00:04:43.792 --> 00:04:45.242
We have a lot to juggle.

00:04:45.242 --> 00:04:47.410
We're trying to get over the hurdle

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.522
of getting her out of our bed.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.355
- Oh.

00:04:50.355 --> 00:04:52.104
- [Stephanie] So we have a king size bed,

00:04:52.104 --> 00:04:54.722
but she absolutely feels like the queen.

00:04:54.722 --> 00:04:56.114
She has to be in the center of the bed-

00:04:56.114 --> 00:04:57.448
- But she's not the queen.

00:04:57.448 --> 00:04:58.498
- [Stephanie] She's not the queen.

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.225
She has to be in the center of the bed.

00:05:00.225 --> 00:05:02.878
She'll pat the pillows to
direct us where to sleep.

00:05:02.878 --> 00:05:05.462
And uh, it's a struggle. So-

00:05:05.462 --> 00:05:06.500
- [Zooey] How old is she?

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.780
- [Stephanie] she's two and a half.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.613
- Ooh.

00:05:08.613 --> 00:05:09.446
- [Stephanie] Currently two and a half.

00:05:09.446 --> 00:05:10.560
- [Kelly] Oh, I'll start.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.019
(laughter)

00:05:12.019 --> 00:05:15.651
- I don't believe in
children sleeping in beds.

00:05:15.651 --> 00:05:17.171
When you're married and
you have another person,

00:05:17.171 --> 00:05:20.237
because look, that's your time.

00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:21.112
(audience laughs)

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:21.945
- [Stephanie] Right.

00:05:21.945 --> 00:05:23.715
- [Kelly] Okay. So that's my thing.

00:05:23.715 --> 00:05:25.584
I'm like, you need to,
and also to make them

00:05:25.584 --> 00:05:27.013
feel safe in their environment.

00:05:27.013 --> 00:05:28.462
I'm like, this is your room.

00:05:28.462 --> 00:05:30.275
And first of all, I shared
a room with my brother

00:05:30.275 --> 00:05:32.678
and sister in her apartment, okay.

00:05:32.678 --> 00:05:35.218
One room with all three of
us at one point in my life.

00:05:35.218 --> 00:05:39.405
And I, you should appreciate
that you have a room to go to.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.568
- [Zooey] I got a warning,

00:05:40.568 --> 00:05:43.217
like right when I had my
first, like from a bunch

00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:45.400
of friends whose kids
wouldn't get out their beds

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.931
and they're like don't ever,
ever, ever let them in.

00:05:47.931 --> 00:05:49.638
They'll never leave.

00:05:49.638 --> 00:05:51.768
So I felt like happy that I had that,

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:53.769
you know, that I was, that I was warned.

00:05:53.769 --> 00:05:55.234
But I think it's hard with your first,

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:57.481
'cause you kind of like
have that bonding with them.

00:05:57.481 --> 00:05:58.314
- But it's been 5 years-

00:05:58.314 --> 00:05:59.264
[Crosstalk 05:57:44]

00:05:59.264 --> 00:06:00.315
- Yeah.

00:06:00.315 --> 00:06:01.555
- I think one thing we did that,

00:06:01.555 --> 00:06:03.675
because we were in this
situation that really helped us.

00:06:03.675 --> 00:06:05.125
And especially at two and a half,

00:06:05.125 --> 00:06:06.634
when you know, you're like, they

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:09.237
get their first big boy
bed or big girl bed.

00:06:09.237 --> 00:06:11.169
We would say, "you can only read stories

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:13.796
in your big girl bed or boy bed."

00:06:13.796 --> 00:06:15.118
We can only do tickle monster

00:06:15.118 --> 00:06:16.767
in your big girl bed or a big boy bed.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.260
Cause then would incentivize them.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:19.868
And they were like, ooh
I get, this is cool.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:22.457
If I'm in this space, I
get to do these fun things.

00:06:22.457 --> 00:06:25.468
And I felt like that was
one way of rewarding them

00:06:25.468 --> 00:06:26.856
for staying in their bed, but-

00:06:26.856 --> 00:06:27.689
- [Kelly] That's good.

00:06:27.689 --> 00:06:28.522
- [Zooey] That's good.

00:06:28.522 --> 00:06:29.355
- Yeah.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.488
It's almost like you could,

00:06:30.488 --> 00:06:31.495
maybe you can have a podcast about it.

00:06:31.495 --> 00:06:32.328
- [Kristen] Yeah.

00:06:32.328 --> 00:06:33.764
(laughter)

00:06:33.764 --> 00:06:35.564
- All right. Let's keep going with Shaina.

00:06:35.564 --> 00:06:37.812
So what do you want to talk about, Shaina?

00:06:37.812 --> 00:06:41.423
(audience clapping)

00:06:41.423 --> 00:06:44.242
- Hey Kelly, I'm a mom of twin girls.

00:06:44.242 --> 00:06:47.062
They're six years old and
I also have a newborn.

00:06:47.062 --> 00:06:49.660
Um, he's three months old.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.320
And last year was really hard on everyone,

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.430
you know, with COVID.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.180
And so my husband and I, we really wanted

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.218
to make Christmas extra special.

00:06:57.218 --> 00:06:58.429
We pulled out all the stops.

00:06:58.429 --> 00:07:01.367
We went completely over the
top, you know, with the toys.

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:03.808
Um, just every toy you can think of.

00:07:03.808 --> 00:07:05.078
The house was filled with toys,

00:07:05.078 --> 00:07:06.718
and then at the end of
the day, the only thing

00:07:06.718 --> 00:07:09.099
they wanted to play with
were these fishing poles

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:11.939
that I got for a trip, a
fishing trip with my dad.

00:07:11.939 --> 00:07:14.937
And I was like, okay, you
know, fishing poles. Okay.

00:07:14.937 --> 00:07:18.678
So my question is, should I
go all out again this year?

00:07:18.678 --> 00:07:19.918
Or do we keep it simple?

00:07:19.918 --> 00:07:24.651
What are, what is your advice
for buying gifts for kids?

00:07:24.651 --> 00:07:25.646
- [Kelly] (whispering) What's your advice?

00:07:25.646 --> 00:07:26.479
(Zooey coughing)

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:27.312
- Well we all know With kids

00:07:27.312 --> 00:07:28.760
it's not quality. It's quantity.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.589
Especially when they're six years old.

00:07:30.589 --> 00:07:32.080
So I would say get 'em one thing

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.220
that's like really special
that they've been asking for,

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.760
and then go to the dollar store,

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.040
and just get a whole bunch of,

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.494
cause they just love to unwrap stuff.

00:07:38.494 --> 00:07:39.327
(audience clapping)

00:07:39.327 --> 00:07:40.160
- [Zooey] They just wanna unwrap stuff.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.617
- [Kristen] You know, kids don't
have any long-term memories

00:07:41.617 --> 00:07:43.148
till they're 4, so I think you can really

00:07:43.148 --> 00:07:44.118
save a lot of money and not-

00:07:44.118 --> 00:07:44.951
(laughter)

00:07:44.951 --> 00:07:47.108
- have to fork out any dough for presents.

00:07:47.108 --> 00:07:48.728
And honestly like, don't you feel like

00:07:48.728 --> 00:07:50.150
this last year we all did that?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.088
We like, we bought our kids'
stuff 'cause we were like

00:07:52.088 --> 00:07:53.339
we wanted everybody to feel better.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:55.619
This was really tough, but
it feels like this year

00:07:55.619 --> 00:07:58.168
we can get back into like
making memories with each other

00:07:58.168 --> 00:08:00.888
and do fun stuff, So I think
maybe they're at that age.

00:08:00.888 --> 00:08:02.268
They're at that wonderful age

00:08:02.268 --> 00:08:03.955
where everything is sort of discovery.

00:08:03.955 --> 00:08:05.910
So you can go to like a pumpkin patch

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.710
